    "summary": "I built a closed one-cell enclosure with two louvred vents. A full hex base is shut by covers on the top and bottom and solid edge caps on all six sides. Two Port louvres sit on opposite side ports, slots 0 and 3, so air can pass across the board. The other four ports are closed with port plugs. The final check found no issues, and the parts don't overlap. It uses 15 parts and needs about 572 g of filament and about 14 hours (829 minutes) of printing. The parts list also includes 12 magnets and 12 steel BBs. The checks cover fit only: they don't show how much cooling the vents give or whether the box keeps out water or dust."
  },
